  "action": "relieve_bend",
  "evidence": "Nightly ~3.2dB extra loss at 1550nm (Rx -12.04 day to -15.36 night) with stable Tx rules out TX/attenuator. OTDR at 1625nm shows same single non-reflective point from both ends (43.3km from A = 3.613km from B, total fibre ~46.9km) jumping 0.82 to 7.85dB (A) and -0.57 to 6.46dB (B) day to night. Much larger at 1625 than 1550 = macrobend wavelength dependence. Location maps to SC-11 route 42.093, re-entered 22min before first alarm. Daytime bidirectional avg (0.82-0.57)/2=0.125dB normal proves splice itself good. Reflective connectors stable.",
